{"id": "EUVD-2026-48627", "enisaUuid": "f6484114-4d7b-3d06-9f53-c1bb1bcf6a48", "description": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\ndrm/amd/display: Validate payload length and link_index in dc_process_dmub_aux_transfer_async\n\n[Why&How]\ndc_process_dmub_aux_transfer_async() copies payload->length bytes into a\n16-byte stack buffer (dpaux.data[16]) guarded only by an ASSERT(), which\nis a no-op in release builds. If a caller ever passes length > 16 this\nresults in a stack buffer overflow via memcpy.\n\nAdditionally, link_index is used to dereference dc->links[] without\nbounds checking against dc->link_count, risking an out-of-bounds access.\n\nReplace the ASSERT with a hard runtime check that returns false when\npayload->length exceeds the destination buffer size, and add a bounds\ncheck for link_index before it is used.\n\n(cherry picked from commit ba4caa9fecdf7a38f98c878ad05a8a64148b6881)", "datePublished": "2026-07-24T15:23:06", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-19T20:28:15", "baseScore": 7.0, "baseScoreVersion": "3.1", "baseScoreVector": "CVSS:3.1/AV:L/AC:H/PR:L/UI:N/S:U/C:H/I:H/A:H", "references": ["https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/d6590e3f766e3111dd1beaf88b9384d117acfa6b", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/16a5fa57565afb6bf37e18129921c270c93d8e2b", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/90c398e822ca76e40548df0c061dd4f93ea92d71", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/3265f3ed373fb8048be713aadcdf702579a0e53d", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/1ecde19bfce6535bffddad1139ff466b6d401b8e", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/1c8c6e912f2945b2a3e669afca6b52174b88e86e", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/6c92f6d9600efa3ef0d9e560a2b52776d9803c29"], "aliases": ["GHSA-gjfp-5cfr-xp55", "CVE-2026-64219"], "assigner": "Linux", "epss": 0.14, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "0584c39d-bda9-365e-b64c-09b2d913c074", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "4f8e37dbaf584de6d38f58b3000b0bfd7eaf2ff6 <16a5fa57565afb6bf37e18129921c270c93d8e2b"}, {"id": "3ccf2bb8-922d-3411-9663-e3868a74c980", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.12.92"}, {"id": "459f3187-664a-31e2-bc84-038255671c12", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.1.175"}, {"id": "57a7ea5a-194d-3caf-9242-5d32a099e680", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.6.142"}, {"id": "69b992e3-9448-3120-b9c3-eac86a317950", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 0"}, {"id": "7fe4ba54-0957-3f84-aa48-dd632b213e6e", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.1"}, {"id": "8989cef4-e536-3744-8ab5-48d6c7f30ecf", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.0.11"}, {"id": "9298216d-f659-3ea1-8941-af39ef537ae0", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "5.13"}, {"id": "9a426296-0fc1-3a6f-b59e-2f14aad7e68f", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "4f8e37dbaf584de6d38f58b3000b0bfd7eaf2ff6 <3265f3ed373fb8048be713aadcdf702579a0e53d"}, {"id": "b774b7fe-d05f-391d-aad9-8f536e8d59aa", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "4f8e37dbaf584de6d38f58b3000b0bfd7eaf2ff6 <6c92f6d9600efa3ef0d9e560a2b52776d9803c29"}, {"id": "c7859558-f37c-383d-9b42-7b0586973d8d", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "4f8e37dbaf584de6d38f58b3000b0bfd7eaf2ff6 <1ecde19bfce6535bffddad1139ff466b6d401b8e"}, {"id": "c970af1a-f555-3c92-be72-ce7310e1b115", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.18.34"}, {"id": "cc8cd796-74dd-3349-a768-e0cd8ef01f08", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "4f8e37dbaf584de6d38f58b3000b0bfd7eaf2ff6 <1c8c6e912f2945b2a3e669afca6b52174b88e86e"}, {"id": "d34e1966-b7